# bug: Subscription function keeps running on the server even after client disconnects (sse) · Issue #5917 · trpc/trpc
created: 2024-07-25, last updated: 2025-06-15, [Read more](https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/5917)

Subscription function on the server side keeps running even after client disconnects.
Server code:
```
stream: sessionProcedure.subscription(async function* () {
let i = 0;
while (true) {
yield i++;
console.log(i);
await Bun.sleep(1000);
}
}),
```
I'm using
```
unstable_httpSubscriptionLink
```
in the client side.
...
To workaround, I'm using
```
ctx.req.signal
```
to break out infinite while loop.
```
stream: sessionProcedure.subscription(async function* ({ ctx }) {
let i = 0;
while (true) {
if (ctx.req.signal.aborted) {
break;
}
yield i++;
await Bun.sleep(1000);
}
}),
...
Unfortunately, we don't have the capacity to assist with issues without a reproduction repository and this issue does not seem to be related to tRPC itself.

